{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "rule": "no_dropped_specific",
 "category": "completeness",
 "family": "no_dropped_specific",
 "positiveClass": "fail",
 "definition": "no_dropped_specific — an answer against the earlier answers to its own case. A specific is a run of letters and digits, joined across a single . : - _ @ / or + that sits between two of them, that holds a digit or is an email address; or a web address read from its http:// or https:// to the next space, quote or closing bracket; a comma joins only as a thousands separator; all read without regard to case, a pure number in one written form (1,050.00 is 1050) and a pure number of one digit never one. An answer written as JSON is read by the values it carries. With k of the m most recent earlier answers to the case (at most 20, newest first) carrying a specific, its share is (k + 1) / (m + 2). A specific is USUAL when its share is three quarters or more (4 · (k + 1) ≥ 3 · (m + 2)), counting only earlier runs that stored an answer. The rule FAILS when this answer does not carry a usual specific. It SKIPS below three earlier runs with an answer (insufficient_history) and when no specific is usual. A measurement: it reports and never decides the verdict. Positive = the answer dropped a usual specific (the rule should FAIL).",
 "source": "Authored 2026-11-10. Synthetic histories, each listing the specifics its earlier answers carried, and an answer written out so the reading of a specific is exercised: figures with separators and trailing zeros, a date, a time, an email address, a web address, an identifier, a one-digit number, an answer written as JSON. Every label follows from the count stated in the note.",
 "labelling": "Labelled 2026-11-10 against the documented definition by counting, in a script that imports nothing from Iris: each note states how many of the earlier runs did the thing and the share the label follows from. A conformance family: it measures that the formula is implemented as written, not what a departure is worth. What a fire is worth is measured on AgentDojo runs and published in proof/OUTSIDE.md.",
 "labelBasis": "definition",
 "authored": "2026-11-10",
